scope: |
  `ci.yml`'s `validate` job fails at a step and SKIPS every step after it. Measured over the last
  twelve ci.yml runs: validate failed on EVERY one since 2026-08-05, the failing step MOVES
  (13 bench-seed -> 8 BUGS-header -> 10 path-area-map -> 9 TASK-regions), and the number of steps
  skipped behind it has grown 11 -> 25.

  THE JOB HEADER'S COVERAGE CLAIM IS FALSE, and that is what makes this matter. It says "Every gate
  this job runs is also in the smoke suite", offered as the reason taking the job off push was safe
  rather than a coverage cut. Measured: 13 of 29 steps are in `scripts/smoke-ci.ssc`, 16 are NOT —
  `build-rust-refuses-loudly`, `launcher-digest-gate`, `std-import-lanes-gate`, three rust parity
  gates, `http-bind-address-gate` and others. Those sixteen have no home anywhere else, so while
  validate is red they are not run at all.

  THE FIX IS SAFE, MEASURED BEFORE PROPOSING IT: all 29 steps run locally on this tree and 28 pass.
  The only red is the path→area map (board-ownership drift, somebody else's routing backlog). So
  making the steps run to completion reveals no hidden pile — it restores 25 checks and leaves the
  one red already visible today.

  NARROW: `if: always()` on the verification steps of ONE job so a red stops hiding its successors,
  plus the entry with the census. The board-ownership backlog is NOT fixed here — it is the current
  occupant, not the defect.
next: plan the task into SPRINT.md, then implement
